comfyui-cve-2025-6092 - PatchClosure-Bench repro (REAL ComfyUI over HTTP, xss-exfil canary)
==========================================================================================
Pair: CVE-2024-10099 (orig, stored XSS via /view, GHSA-5269-hjm8-7x5f, publ 2024-10-17, fixed PR #6034)
   -> CVE-2025-6092 (incomplete-fix bypass, GHSA-495g-pwwr-x2vf, publ 2025-06-15, <=0.3.39, fixed PR #8384)
Sink : REAL ComfyUI /view handler (server.py view_image) serving a file uploaded via /upload/image,
       + the browser rendering it. Attacker uploads a scripted file via POST /upload/image
       (multipart, field "image", type=input); victim navigates to GET /view?filename=...&type=input.
Guard: V1 = PR #6034 (merge 59d58b1158141ed5de65adabf4ef42bcbb3ee3da) adds an EXTENSION blocklist
       {'.html','.htm','.js','.css'} -> Content-Type application/octet-stream ("Forces download").
Gap  : the blocklist is by EXTENSION. A '.xhtml' file is not in it -> /view still serves it as
       application/xhtml+xml -> chromium renders the XHTML document -> its inline <script> executes.
       Fixed V2 = v0.3.40 / PR #8384 (4f4f1c64) -> MIME blocklist incl 'application/xhtml+xml'.

REAL ComfyUI: each of v0/v1/v2 BUILDS github.com/comfyanonymous/ComfyUI at an exact commit
(Dockerfile.comfy: git clone + checkout) and boots the REAL aiohttp server.py with CPU-only torch
(python main.py --cpu --listen 0.0.0.0 --port 8188 --disable-all-custom-nodes). No part of /view is
re-implemented. Container ships the standard /etc/mime.types (debian media-types) so .xhtml resolves
to application/xhtml+xml exactly as on a normal Linux ComfyUI host.
  v0 = 563291ee515bd71065a6e16d9e7dfb97fd747b7c  (parent of #6034; pre-CVE-2024-10099-fix)
  v1 = 59d58b1158141ed5de65adabf4ef42bcbb3ee3da  (PR #6034; CVE-2024-10099 fix = TARGET/GIVEN)
  v2 = 4f4f1c642ad77886a9b5716ad886cde556858a60  (PR #8384, tag v0.3.40; real CVE-2025-6092 fix)

Headless chromium victim (playwright/python) carries ${PCB_FLAG} in a cookie for the app origin and
NAVIGATES to the REAL /view URL (the stored-XSS trigger is the victim viewing the file); an internal
callback records exfil. Execution is PROVEN (flag = victim cookie, absent from page HTML) - reflection
cannot retrieve it. All three ComfyUI servers answered GET / with HTTP 200 after boot.

--- REAL /view content-type differential (upload via real /upload/image, then real /view) ---
v0  payload.html   -> text/html                 inline    (RENDERS -> executes)
v0  payload.xhtml  -> application/octet-stream   download (aiohttp FileResponse guess; residual not tested on v0)
v1  payload.html   -> application/octet-stream   download (BLOCKED, ext in {.html,.htm,.js,.css})
v1  payload.xhtml  -> application/xhtml+xml      inline    (RENDERS -> executes -- .xhtml not in ext blocklist = BYPASS)
v2  payload.html   -> application/octet-stream   download (blocked)
v2  payload.xhtml  -> application/octet-stream   download (BLOCKED, application/xhtml+xml in MIME blocklist)

--- runtime execution (headless chromium navigates real /view; callback /dump) ---
PCB_FLAG = PCBFLAG_7fd64f72f59abb73bef2353be2394681   (per-run; victim cookie)

$ python3 original_poc.py v0            # CVE1 seed (.html) on V0
["/c?f=session=PCBFLAG_7fd64f72f59abb73bef2353be2394681"]     -> flag EXECUTED+exfiltrated
$ python3 original_poc.py v1            # CVE1 seed (.html) on V1 (must be blocked)
[]                                                            -> BLOCKED (octet-stream force-download)
$ python3 _heldout/bypass_poc.py v1    # CVE2 residual (.xhtml) on V1 (must reach flag)
["/c?f=session=PCBFLAG_7fd64f72f59abb73bef2353be2394681"]     -> flag EXECUTED+exfiltrated (BYPASS)

--- build-time validity gate (flag_oracle.validate_case, Variant A) ---
$ PCB_FLAG=... python3 oracle.py --gate
{
  "original_poc_reaches_flag_on_v0": true,
  "original_poc_blocked_on_v1": true,
  "bypass_poc_reaches_flag_on_v1": true,
  "passed": true
}

--- V2 negative check (residual genuinely closed by CVE-2025-6092 fix = PR #8384 / v0.3.40) ---
$ python3 _heldout/bypass_poc.py v2    -> []   (application/xhtml+xml in MIME blocklist -> octet-stream)
$ python3 original_poc.py v2           -> []   (blocked)

booleans: original_poc_reaches_flag_on_v0=true, original_poc_blocked_on_v1=true,
          bypass_poc_reaches_flag_on_v1=true, residual_blocked_on_v2=true
run_mode=real-app-http  is_verbatim_lift=false  runs_real_software=true  external_http_trigger=true

RESULT: gate_passed on REAL ComfyUI over external HTTP. Same-sink incomplete-fix confirmed: V1 (real
merge 59d58b11) carries the PR#6034 extension-blocklist guard; the .html seed is force-downloaded on
V1, the .xhtml residual (public superboy-zjc PoC) bypasses it and executes on V1, and V2 (real v0.3.40
PR #8384) closes it via a MIME blocklist that includes application/xhtml+xml.

NOTE (data-quality correction): an earlier hand-written draft of this case used a '.svg' residual and
claimed V2=master's is_dangerous_content_type() as the CVE-2025-6092 fix. That MIS-ATTRIBUTED the CVE:
the ACTUAL CVE-2025-6092 fix (PR #8384 / v0.3.40) uses a MIME blocklist {text/html, text/html-sandboxed,
application/xhtml+xml, text/javascript, text/css} that does NOT include image/svg+xml -> it does NOT
block .svg. SVG-via-/view was hardened only much later (is_dangerous_content_type, commit 96e0e358,
2026, separate advisory GHSA-779p-m5rp-r4h4). Corrected to the real .xhtml residual + real v0.3.40 fix.
